    tenth = '<section id="tenth-pass"><h2>Preview recovery, pointer alignment and a color finding</h2><p>The resumed stage carried earlier evidence forward. Candidate <code>' + html.escape(summary10['loaded_build']) + '</code> retires an excluded preview lane when its helper changes identity, rejects a request while the helper is absent, and resolves a fresh lane after relaunch. The unrelated lane remained available. Fifteen mechanical checks and two targeted MCP tests passed.</p><p>One combined fixture take supplied <strong>481 exact source/mux timestamps</strong> and four app-delivered native clicks across 1×/2× displays. Raw coordinates and event timestamps matched the app exactly; all four predicted marker positions matched actual video within <strong>0.5 pixels</strong>. Initial native delivery refused; an exposed move control recovered it, and the same take was kept. Requested screenshot coordinates were not assumed equal to delivered points.</p><p class="note"><strong>Cross-display color fidelity needs correction.</strong> Six declared sRGB references differed by at most two channel values on Retina, but by as much as 76 on the external display. Returning home restored the initial values. Capture already requests sRGB; the actual buffer metadata/pixel format and writer conversion need isolation before choosing a fix. The software preview reproduced all 18 sampled parent RGB values exactly, including the inaccurate colors.</p><div class="pair">'
